' Tour slide 10 — "Who needs what from the system?"
' Use-case diagram over the SAME course-registration territory. Plan §S s10.
' "Drop a course" carries the single accent in the figure: it returns on slide 27
' (Models refine into models) as the use case the refinement chain starts from.
' The accent is a DEEPER SLATE fill at the same rim weight. It must not be the warm #faf7f0:
' that cream already means "decision / branch" in the sequence and activity diagrams
' (the alt frame, the capacity diamond), and reusing it here would read as semantics.
' It must not be red either — #C8102E is reserved deck-wide for the Modeling-lever overlay.
@startuml
!include _theme.puml
left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 150
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #fdfcf9
  BorderColor #2f5169
  BorderThickness 2
  FontColor #41586c
  FontSize 27
}

actor Student as ST
actor Instructor as IN
actor Registrar as RG

rectangle "Course registration" {
  usecase UC1 as "Register for\na section"
  usecase UC2 as "Drop a course" #d7e3ed
  usecase UC3 as "View roster"
  usecase UC4 as "Approve a\ncourse proposal"
}

ST --> UC1
ST --> UC2
IN --> UC3
RG --> UC4
@enduml
